problems.statement:
The fundamental infrared absorption band of hydrogen chloride ($^1	ext{H}^{35}	ext{Cl}$) has its band origin (missing Q-branch) at wavenumber $ ar{
u}_0 = 2885.9	ext{ cm}^{-1}$. (a) Calculate the fundamental vibrational frequency $
u_0$ in Hz and the effective chemical bond force constant $k$ in N/m (reduced mass $\mu = 1.6267 	imes 10^{-27}	ext{ kg}$). (b) Compute the zero-point vibrational energy (ZPE) of the molecule in eV. (c) Predict the fundamental vibrational wavenumber $ ar{
u}_0'$ for deuterium chloride ($^2	ext{H}^{35}	ext{Cl}$) assuming the same force constant.
